Original commit body from df642be:

Previously, `symbols --exclude-tests` hid test symbols from display but
still counted test edges when computing in-degree and out-degree. This
led to inflated degree counts that were inconsistent with what `explain -x`
showed for the same symbols.

Now when --exclude-tests is set, edges where either src or dst is a test
file are excluded from degree computation, making the counts consistent
across commands.
